The small garden, splendid pond, brilliantly connect;
Thoughts are endless by the back door, the front threshold.
Consort Mi's slender waist barely胜过 the dew;
Empress Zhao, body light, wishes to lean on the wind.
The red wall is silent, cliff honey exhausted;
The blue curtain stretches far, the misty nest is empty.
Green Mound's powder butterflies, cease your parting grief;
We are fated to meet again in the second month.

【Silkworm】

Hearing Orioles at Baitian While on Horseback
Li Bai
Orioles peck purple mulberries,
In May they sing on mulberry branches.
My journey's days I do not mark,
Mistaking it for springtime.
The silkworms are old, the traveler未 returns;
At Baitian, silk is already reeled.
Driving my horse onward again,
I touch my heart,空自 sorrow.

【Cicada】

Cicada
Yu Shinan
Drooping tassels drink the clear dew;
The flowing sound emerges from sparse paulownia.
High perch, the voice carries far of itself;
It is not by relying on the autumn wind.

Chanting on the Cicada While in Prison
Luo Binwang
The western陆 cicada's song resounds;
The southern冠 prisoner's thoughts run deep.
I cannot bear this dark-temple shadow,
Coming to face my white-haired chant.
Heavy dew, hard to fly forward;
Much wind, the sound easily sinks.
No one believes in lofty purity;
Who will speak for my heart?

Cicada
Li Shangyin
Originally, because of height, it's hard to be full;
In vain, it resents wasting its voice.
